<title>TURKEY: Turk Tat H1 net profit triples.</title>
<headline>Turk Tat H1 net profit triples.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-June 1997 final</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit   367.78     vs   297.58</p>
<p>    Net Profit	   827.52     vs   267.82</p>
<p>    Net sales	  5,280.52     vs 2,479.09</p>
<p>    Operating profit 1,460.94     vs   674.76</p>
<p>    Exceptional income 332.85     vs   270.43</p>
<p>    Interest paid	670.14     vs   466.35</p>
<p>    Total debts	4,138.14     vs 2,589.88</p>
<p>    Equity	     5,283.54     vs 2,493.74</p>
<p>    Capital	    2,250.00     vs   900.00</p>
<p>NOTE-Tat Konserve Sanayii A.S is Turkey's biggest tomato paste producer  and exporter.It also makes canned and frozen vegetables and fruits.</p>
<p>Its major shareholders are leading Turkish industrial conglomerate  Koc with 46.36 percent stake and Japanese Kagome Co Ltd with 10.64  percent.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 78 percent consumer  price inflation in June.</p>
<p>--Istanbul Newsroom +90-212 275 08 75</p>
</text>
